# Code owners for krt-profit/basetool.
#
# GitHub reads this file to decide who is automatically requested for review on
# a pull request. It is REVIEW ROUTING, not an access-control mechanism: an
# entry here grants nobody any permission, and it only becomes a merge gate if
# branch protection on `main` has "Require review from Code Owners" enabled.
# Owning a path therefore costs nothing except a review request.
#
# Syntax notes that bite:
#   - Patterns are gitignore-style. `docs/` matches the whole tree; `/docs/`
#     anchors at the repository root; `*.md` matches at every depth.
#   - THE LAST MATCHING RULE WINS — unlike .gitignore, rules do not accumulate.
#     A file matched by both `*` and `/scripts/deploy.sh` is owned by whoever
#     the LATER line names, and by them alone. Order the stanzas from broad to
#     narrow, and never re-broaden further down the file.
#   - An owner must have write access to the repository, or GitHub silently
#     drops the rule rather than reporting an error.
#   - GitHub never requests a review from the pull request's own author, so a
#     maintainer opening a PR against a path they own is not blocked by it.
#
# The repository currently has a single maintainer, so every stanza names the
# same owner. The paths are still spelled out rather than collapsed into one
# `*` line: they document which surfaces are considered high-risk, and they
# keep working unchanged when a second maintainer is added — that change then
# becomes a one-line edit per area instead of a rewrite.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default owner for everything not matched by a more specific rule below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                   @greluc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supply chain and CI/CD.
#
# These files decide what gets built, what gets signed, what is attested and
# what reaches the production host. A change here can compromise every artifact
# the project publishes without touching a single line of application code, so
# they are called out explicitly rather than left to the `*` default.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/                           @greluc
/.github/workflows/                 @greluc
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @greluc
/.github/dependabot.yml             @greluc

# The deploy path: the host pulls and applies whatever these produce
# (REQ-OPS-001, REQ-OPS-015). deploy.sh runs as a docker-group user, i.e.
# root-equivalent on the production box.
/scripts/                           @greluc
/docker/                            @greluc
/docker-compose*.yml                @greluc
/monitoring/                        @greluc

# Build definition and dependency pins. `gradle/libs.versions.toml` is the
# single place dependency versions are declared, so it is the single place a
# malicious or careless version change would land.
/build.gradle.kts                   @greluc
/settings.gradle.kts                @greluc
/gradle/                            @greluc
/gradlew                            @greluc
/gradlew.bat                        @greluc
/config/                            @greluc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binding governance documents.
#
# Specs and ADRs are binding per CLAUDE.md — code may not silently contradict
# them, and amending one is how a requirement legitimately changes. The role
# matrix is the authoritative statement of who may do what. Licensing, the CLA
# and the security policy carry legal weight.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/docs/specs/                        @greluc
/docs/adr/                          @greluc
/ROLES_AND_PERMISSIONS.md           @greluc
/.github/SECURITY.md                @greluc
/LICENSE.md                         @greluc
/CLA.md                             @greluc
/CONTRIBUTING.md                    @greluc
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md                 @greluc
/CLAUDE.md                          @greluc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security-critical application code.
#
# Authorization is centralised in @PreAuthorize plus OwnerScopeService, and the
# multi-org-unit scoping is what keeps one squadron's data out of another's
# (REQ-SEC-*, REQ-ORG-*). Flyway migrations are irreversible in production.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/backend/src/main/java/de/greluc/krt/profit/basetool/backend/config/       @greluc
/backend/src/main/resources/db/migration/                                  @greluc
/frontend/src/main/java/de/greluc/krt/profit/basetool/frontend/config/     @greluc
/keycloak-spi/                                                             @greluc
/keycloak-theme/                                                           @greluc
